  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A rod of mass <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"6.0\\; \\textup{kg}\"></span> and length <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2.0\\; \\textup{m}\"></span>, initially at rest, is rotated by a constant force <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F\"></span> about its centre.</p>\n\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure>\n\n<p>After <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"20\"></span> seconds, the angular momentum of the rod is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"10\\; \\textup{kg\\,m}^{2} \\textup{\\,s}^{-1}\"></span>. The moment of inertia for the rod is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"I = \\frac{1}{12}mL^{2}\"></span>, where <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"m\"></span> is the mass and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"L\"></span> is the length of the rod.</p>\n<p>What is the best estimate for the number of full revolutions completed by the rod?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"8\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"16\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"50\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"100\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
  },
